invariant: INV-16
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile stops refusing the CHACHA variable, so a build that still
  passes CHACHA=vector for a raw client gets the portable loop with no
  word said, where its builder expects the vector path.
  lint-trust-separation's refused rows require make print-lib-def to
  fail for CHACHA=vector and CHACHA=portable, on a device object and on a
  host object.

--- old
ifneq ($(origin CHACHA),undefined)
--- new
ifneq (,)
